1
00:00:06,900 --> 00:00:12,600
Floor Plan 2027 is a home-design program that runs in your web browser. Nothing to install.

2
00:00:12,700 --> 00:00:21,017
You draw a house as a 2D floor plan: walls, doors, windows, stairs, furniture, roof and garden.

3
00:00:21,150 --> 00:00:24,350
Then you look at it in 3D, from any angle, with the click of a button.

4
00:00:28,750 --> 00:00:35,650
Every object has real measurements, so the plan and the 3D model always match.

5
00:00:35,783 --> 00:00:39,983
Your plan is saved in the browser as you work, and can be saved to a file or exported as a picture.

6
00:00:40,133 --> 00:00:43,133
Let's take a tour of the screen. This is a new, empty plan.

7
00:00:43,233 --> 00:00:49,533
The top bar: the plan's name, the floor tabs, and the Wizard, Demo and File buttons.

8
00:00:49,633 --> 00:00:55,933
On the left, the icon library: 151 icons in categories — walls, doors, windows, stairs, furniture, garden…

9
00:00:56,033 --> 00:01:02,633
Type in the search box to find an icon quickly. Right-click any icon for a 3D preview of it.

10
00:01:02,733 --> 00:01:10,233
Above the plan, the toolbar: undo and redo, zoom, display options, helpers like Snap and Align, and the 3D view button.

11
00:01:10,333 --> 00:01:14,533
In the middle, the drawing area, on a grid. Scroll to zoom; drag an empty spot to move around.

12
00:01:14,633 --> 00:01:21,833
On the right, Properties: the settings of whatever you have selected — or of the whole plan when nothing is.

13
00:01:21,933 --> 00:01:27,933
The thin Height bar shows the floor you are working on and its height above the ground.

14
00:01:28,033 --> 00:01:34,033
And along the bottom, the status bar: the pointer position, what is selected, and handy tips.

15
00:01:34,133 --> 00:01:38,633
There are three ways to start: watch a demo, let the Wizard design a house, or draw your own.

16
00:01:38,767 --> 00:01:43,517
The quickest way to learn: watch a house being built. Click Demo.

17
00:01:43,617 --> 00:01:49,067
Pick a sample house. Let's choose the Garden cottage.

18
00:01:49,167 --> 00:01:54,767
The house is built in the order a real house is: first the outer walls…

19
00:01:54,867 --> 00:02:02,967
Click Next for each step. The objects a step adds stay selected, so you can see what was built.

20
00:02:03,067 --> 00:02:06,667
Each step is explained in the panel at the bottom. Previous goes back a step.

21
00:02:06,767 --> 00:02:09,917
Click Play to let it build the rest by itself.

22
00:02:33,017 --> 00:02:41,417
Finished! Keep this house makes it your own plan to change. Exit demo brings your own plan back.

23
00:02:41,567 --> 00:02:46,067
Want a house of your own design, fast? Click Wizard.

24
00:02:46,167 --> 00:02:53,217
The House Building Wizard asks a few questions. Start with a name and the surroundings.

25
00:02:53,317 --> 00:02:58,517
The picture on the right updates as you answer: a front view and the floor layouts.

26
00:02:58,617 --> 00:03:02,367
Size: how big the house is on the ground.

27
00:03:02,467 --> 00:03:06,417
Storeys: one, two or three floors, and how high each one is.

28
00:03:06,517 --> 00:03:12,917
Rooms: how many bedrooms and bathrooms. Let's ask for 4 bedrooms.

29
00:03:13,017 --> 00:03:21,267
Then wall colours, the roof, floor finishes and extras. Every answer can be changed later.

30
00:03:21,367 --> 00:03:25,917
The last step sums it all up. Click Build the house.

31
00:03:26,017 --> 00:03:30,117
It is built step by step, just like the demo. Let's play it through.

32
00:03:57,217 --> 00:04:02,967
To change your answers, click ✎ Change answers. Happy with it? Click Keep this house.

33
00:04:03,067 --> 00:04:06,467
The house is now your plan — every wall and piece of furniture can be edited.

34
00:04:06,600 --> 00:04:12,000
Now let's draw a plan ourselves. Open the File menu and choose New plan…

35
00:04:13,100 --> 00:04:18,600
Set the number of floors and their heights here — the defaults are fine. Click Create plan.

36
00:04:18,700 --> 00:04:25,750
To add something, drag its icon onto the plan. Let's start with a Room: four walls in one go.

37
00:04:25,850 --> 00:04:29,450
It is selected: blue handles appear around it, and its Properties show on the right.

38
00:04:29,550 --> 00:04:33,400
Type exact sizes in Properties. Length 5 m…

39
00:04:33,500 --> 00:04:36,150
…and width 4 m.

40
00:04:36,250 --> 00:04:39,450
You can also drag the handles to resize, and drag the room itself to move it.

41
00:04:39,550 --> 00:04:43,850
Next, a door. Type door in the search box…

42
00:04:43,950 --> 00:04:53,000
…and drag the door onto a wall. Align fits it into the wall automatically.

43
00:04:54,100 --> 00:04:56,500
A window goes into the wall the same way.

44
00:04:56,600 --> 00:05:04,250
Now some furniture: a double bed…

45
00:05:04,350 --> 00:05:08,150
…and a sofa.

46
00:05:08,250 --> 00:05:12,600
Drag an object to move it. Snap keeps it on the grid.

47
00:05:12,700 --> 00:05:16,100
Press R to rotate the selected object by 90°.

48
00:05:16,200 --> 00:05:19,200
Ctrl + D duplicates it…

49
00:05:19,300 --> 00:05:22,100
…Delete removes it…

50
00:05:22,200 --> 00:05:27,500
…and Ctrl + Z undoes anything. Let's undo the rotation too.

51
00:05:27,600 --> 00:05:33,900
Last, a floor. Click Fill floor, then click inside the room.

52
00:05:33,000 --> 00:05:39,000
The floor fills the room exactly. Choose its material on the right — wood, tiles, carpet, stone…

53
00:05:40,133 --> 00:05:43,833
Ready to see it? Click 3D view.

54
00:05:43,967 --> 00:05:46,967
Drag to turn around the house. Scroll to zoom in and out.

55
00:05:51,967 --> 00:05:59,567
Cut walls lowers the walls so you can look into the rooms.

56
00:05:59,700 --> 00:06:10,633
Top looks straight down; Eye level stands you inside, 2 m above the floor.

57
00:06:10,767 --> 00:06:16,567
Any change you make on the plan shows up in 3D. Close 3D (or Esc) goes back.

58
00:06:16,733 --> 00:06:22,183
Give your plan a name: click the name at the top left and type.

59
00:06:22,283 --> 00:06:26,283
Your plan is saved in this browser automatically as you work — close the tab and it is still there next time.

60
00:06:26,383 --> 00:06:31,283
To keep a copy, share it, or move it to another computer, use the File menu.

61
00:06:31,383 --> 00:06:35,783
Save (Ctrl + S) downloads the plan as a .json file; Open… loads it again.

62
00:06:35,883 --> 00:06:39,883
Export SVG or Export PNG saves a picture of the drawing to print or send.

